```
Reason:
The bug occurs because the driver module reference count is not incremented when accessing the Type-C mux or switch devices. This can lead to the driver being unloaded while still in use, causing potential kernel paging errors when the system attempts to access the unloaded driver.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
